---
/** /affiliate-disclosure/: how affiliate links and ads pay for the site. */
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import TrustLayout from '~/layouts/TrustLayout.astro';

const retailers = site.retailers.map((r) => r.name).join(' and ');
---

<TrustLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description={`How ${site.name} earns money from retailer links and ads, and why it never changes our ratings.`}
  path="/affiliate-disclosure/"
  updated={site.legal.updated}
>
  <div class="prose max-w-[72ch]">
    <p>
      {site.name} is free to read. We pay for testing and writing with affiliate commissions and
      display ads.
    </p>
    <h2 id="affiliate-links">Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Buttons and links to retailers such as {retailers} are affiliate links. If you buy something
      after following one, the retailer may pay us a small commission. You pay the same price either
      way, and the retailer does not tell us who you are.
    </p>
    <p>
      We add affiliate links after a review or guide is written. Whether a retailer pays a
      commission plays no part in what we recommend, the score we give or the order of a list. When
      a product is cheaper at a retailer that pays us nothing, we still show that price.
    </p>
    <h2 id="ads">Ads</h2>
    <p>
      We show display ads from Google AdSense on articles and listings, only after you accept
      cookies. Ads are labelled "Advertisement" and never placed inside verdicts, scores or buy
      buttons. There are no ads on this page or our other policy pages. See our{' '}
      <a href="/privacy/#cookies">privacy policy</a>
      for the cookies ads use.
    </p>
    <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Read our <a href="/review-policy/">review policy</a>, or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</TrustLayout>
